        <ArticleTitle>Reasoned interpretation of a longitudinal intervention</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Longitudinal evidence can distinguish a persistent association from a transient response to measurement.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">The intervention group retained a modest improvement after adjustment for the prespecified baseline differences. Nevertheless, uncertainty in the final estimate limits strong causal interpretation of this association.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
