        <ArticleTitle>Independent replication across clinical settings</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>The replicated association remained directionally consistent across three independently sampled clinical settings. Because the confidence intervals overlap, the apparent heterogeneity should be interpreted cautiously rather than as decisive evidence of effect modification.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
